- **Hindsight coding agents** — `@vectorize-io/hindsight-coding-agents`
  (https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight), installed separately by its own
  command and not redistributed here. Its staged runtime under `~/.hindsight/` and
  its companion skill under `~/.agents/skills/` are governed by that project's
  license.

- **RTK** — `rtk` 1.1.0, installed separately as a standalone binary
  (https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk) and invoked by `@cc/dsh-rtk`; no RTK code is
  vendored or redistributed here. This deployment installs the **`rtk-oss`
  edition**, which is Apache-2.0 only: the kit needs the command filters, and the
  permissive edition keeps every dependency it ships around permissive. Upstream's
  default download adds `rtk-engine` (BUSL-1.1, source-available, with a
  production-use grant that covers running the binary); switching is one variable,
  `RTK_EDITION`, and the plugin behaves the same under either edition.

- **Headroom** — `headroom-ai` 0.41.0, installed separately with `uv` or `pip`
  (https://github.com/headroomlabs-ai/headroom, Apache-2.0) and run as a local
  proxy; not redistributed here. The kit disables its anonymous usage beacon
  (`HEADROOM_BEACON=off`) and its tool-schema deferral (`HEADROOM_TOOL_SEARCH=0`).

- **SkillClaw** — no SkillClaw code is installed or redistributed.
  `@cc/dsh-skill-evolve` is this repository's own implementation of the skill
  evolution and dedupe behaviour that SkillClaw (https://github.com/AMAP-ML/SkillClaw)
  motivated, and it writes the same `SKILL.md` format SkillClaw's library uses.

- **Babysitter** — `@a5c-ai/babysitter` 6.x, installed separately with npm
  (https://github.com/a5c-ai/babysitter, MIT) and invoked by `@cc/dsh-babysitter`;
  not redistributed here.

The harness itself (`@deepseek-ai/dsh`) is installed separately with npm. The
runtime dependencies its bundles pull in (for example `node-pty`, `ws` and
xterm.js) are installed with it and are not redistributed in this repository.
